  "body": "I frequently want to build a new list based on an old one by modifying the old list's elements using substeps. Perhaps:\r\n\r\n> 1. Let *newList* be the result of **transforming** each *item* of *oldList* through the following steps:\r\n>    1. **Return** *item* + 2.\r\n\r\nas shorthand for:\r\n\r\n> 1. Let *newList* be a new **list**.\r\n> 1. **For each** *item* of *oldList*:\r\n>    1. **Append** *item* + 2 to *newList*.\r\n\r\n\"Return\" could be \"include\" or \"append\" or some other term.\r\n\r\nThe text I'm proposing isn't much shorter, but it keeps the logical operation in a single step instead of spreading it across 2.",
